From 43303da8bc6945fb3e0af47b4b03f5c862b9e1e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:10:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rendervulkan: add a fragment shader composite path

With --composite-graphics or GAMESCOPE_COMPOSITE_GRAPHICS=1 the output
is written by a fullscreen fragment pass instead of a compute dispatch.
The blit, RCAS, blur and conditional blur passes get fragment variants.
The upscaler passes before them stay on compute.

The output images then drop STORAGE usage and become colour attachments.
turnip refuses UBWC for storage images before a7xx, so this is what lets
the scanned-out buffer stay compressed. The shaders map each output
pixel back to its scene coordinate, and on a tiler that makes rotating
to the panel free.

If the blit pipeline can't be built for the output formats, compositing
falls back to compute. Screenshots and the upscale cache stay on
compute, and the composite debug markers are off on this path because
they need image stores.
